```

The assert `2 * H5F_SIZEOF_ADDR(f) <= H5G_SIZEOF_SCRATCH` checks that 2 × sizeof_addr <= 16. For sizeof_addr=16, 2 × 16 = 32 > 16, so the assert fails. But in release builds, the assert is disabled.

Then `H5F_addr_decode` is called twice, each reading 16 bytes. So it reads 32 bytes total for the addresses. But the scratch pad is only 16 bytes. So it reads 16 bytes past the end of the entry.

Now, the entry is at the end of the superblock buffer. So reading past the end of the entry reads past the end of the buffer. This is the heap-buffer-overflow READ.

